hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"180","Al-hamdu lillāhi alladhī aṭ'amānī hādhā wa razaqanīhi min ghayri ḥawlin minnī wa lā quwwah.. Praise be to Allah who fed me this and provided it for me without any power or strength from myself."
"181","Alhamdu lillāhi ḥamdan kathīran tayyiban mubārakan fīh, ghayra makfiyyin wa lā muwadda`in, wa lā mustaghnan `anhu Rabbanā. All praise is to Allah, praise in abundance, good and blessed. It cannot [be compensated for, nor can it] be left, nor can it be done without, our Lord. Reference: Al-Bukhari 6/214, At-Tirmidhi 5/507."
